# SABOTAGE: T181 (ADR-047 §10a row 25) gate sabotage — the hook seam's FAIL-CLOSED rescue
# is dropped. `Samen.AI.Agent.Hooks.safe_call/3` no longer converts a raising / throwing /
# exiting / non-exporting hook into the strongest refusal its point accepts; it converts it
# into `:ok`, i.e. "this hook had no opinion". The chain then defers and the loop executes
# the governed tool call UNHOOKED — a broken policy hook stops being a refusal and becomes
# a bypass, which is exactly the silent degrade this seam exists to prevent. The named reds
# (the loop-level red proving the tool never executes unhooked, and the unit-level red
# proving a raise fails closed to the strongest refusal the point accepts) MUST flip; the
# passing remainder of the suite is the control proving the rescue is not blanket-failing
# every hook path.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/ai/agent_hooks_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: the tool never executes UNHOOKED
# MUST_FAIL: a raise fails closed to the STRONGEST refusal the point accepts
